<%- include('partials/head') %>
<%- include('partials/header') %>

<main style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--nc-layout-gap);">
  <section class="card">
    <div class="card-header">
      <div>
        <h1 class="card-title nc-type-headline-medium" tabindex="-1">Recovery Submission Received (Prototype)</h1>
        <p class="card-desc nc-type-body-medium">
          Demonstration for Task 3 Step 5: Password reset recovery code verification prototype.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--nc-space-3); color: var(--nc-color-on-surface-variant);" class="nc-type-body-medium">
      <div style="padding: var(--nc-space-3); border: 1px solid var(--nc-color-outline-variant); border-radius: 4px; background: var(--nc-color-surface-container-high);">
        <p style="color: var(--nc-color-on-surface); font-weight: 600;">Prototype Status</p>
        <p>In this prototype, submitting a code does not check a database, verify single-use tokens, or unlock accounts. The submitted value is handled safely without echoing secret credentials or exposing parameter lengths in the response view.</p>
        <p style="margin-top: var(--nc-space-2); color: var(--nc-color-on-surface);">
          Stronger token generation, expiry windows, attempt limits, and server-side cryptographic verification are treated as future controls.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p style="margin-top: var(--nc-space-4);">
        <a href="/auth/recovery" class="auth-link">&larr; Return to code entry demonstration</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
